    "final_text": "I built the todo CLI and all four commands work. `npm test` runs 103 tests and they all pass. It has no dependencies and needs Node 18 or later.\n\n```\n$ node index.js add \"Buy groceries\"\nAdded todo #1: Buy groceries\n$ node index.js list\n1. [x] Buy groceries\n2. [ ] Walk the dog\n$ node index.js complete abc\nError: Invalid id \"abc\": must be a positive integer      (exit 1)\n```\n\n**Files**\n- `index.js` \u2014 the command-line entry point. It reads the command, prints results, and returns exit code 0 on success or 1 on error.\n- `lib/todos.js` \u2014 reads and writes `todos.json` in the current directory, and does add, complete, delete and list formatting.\n- `package.json` \u2014 `npm test` runs `node --test`.\n- `test/todos.test.js` \u2014 tests for the library functions.\n- `test/cli.test.js` \u2014 runs the real CLI in temporary folders and checks its output, exit codes and what ends up in `todos.json`.\n- `README.md` \u2014 a short usage guide. I also added `todos.json` to `.gitignore` so your todo data doesn't get committed.\n\n**Edge cases handled**\n- **Missing arguments:** an error plus a usage line for that command.\n- **Invalid ids:** `abc`, `0`, `-1`, `1.5`, `1e3` and numbers too large to store exactly are rejected.\n- **Unknown ids and extra arguments:** `complete 99` on a missing todo and `delete 1 2` are errors.\n- **Empty or blank text** is rejected.\n- **Empty list:** `list` prints a friendly message.\n- **Unknown commands** give an error plus the help text.\n- **Damaged `todos.json`:** bad JSON, something that isn't a list, or a malformed entry gives a clear error.\n\nErrors go to stderr, exit with code 1, and never change `todos.json`. Writes go to a temporary file first and then replace the original, so a crash mid-write can't leave the file half-written.\n\n**Choices I made where the spec was open**\n- **Ids:** a new todo gets one more than the highest existing id, and deleting doesn't renumber the others. Deleting the highest-numbered todo does let its id be reused; stopping that would mean storing a counter in the file, and I kept the file as a plain list of todos.\n- **Quotes optional:** `add Buy groceries` works the same as `add \"Buy groceries\"`, and extra spaces around the text are trimmed.\n- **Already done:** completing a todo that's already done prints a notice and exits with code 0 rather than failing.\n- **List layout:** ids are right-aligned so the `[x]`/`[ ]` column lines up once ids reach 10.\n\nTo check the tests actually catch bugs, I broke the code on purpose twice: once to print the wrong status marker, once to reuse ids. They caught it with 3 and 5 failures. My first attempt to put the file back didn't work because `cp` in your shell asks before overwriting. I restored it from the backup and confirmed the original code is in place with all 103 tests passing.\n\nNothing is committed yet; all the changes are in your working tree on `main`.",
